WEBVTT

00:01.460 --> 00:05.690
This will likely be the only year I get 
to compete with Anne in the Exhibition.

00:06.440 --> 00:10.650
I'm lucky enough to have been here 
for Anne's last chance.

00:11.730 --> 00:12.950
Last chance?

00:13.390 --> 00:14.490
That's right.

00:15.410 --> 00:18.470
If she doesn't become 
a silver sugar master this year...

00:19.400 --> 00:21.450
then she may not ever be able to.

00:25.470 --> 00:33.490
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

00:40.180 --> 00:42.910
<i>It's all right</i>

00:42.910 --> 00:46.750
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

00:46.750 --> 00:53.250
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

00:53.250 --> 00:59.830
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

00:59.830 --> 01:09.150
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

01:09.590 --> 01:12.800
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

01:12.800 --> 01:15.930
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

01:16.210 --> 01:23.040
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

01:23.040 --> 01:25.730
<i>That miracle</i>

01:25.980 --> 01:32.690
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

01:32.690 --> 01:38.990
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

01:38.990 --> 01:46.120
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

01:46.120 --> 01:54.350
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

01:59.470 --> 02:00.860
How's it going over there?

02:00.860 --> 02:03.500
Hey! It's time to trade positions!

02:03.500 --> 02:04.220
Got it!

02:04.220 --> 02:06.250
Wow...

02:11.480 --> 02:14.480
It's huge and there's so many artisans!

02:14.480 --> 02:15.360
Yes.

02:19.080 --> 02:19.980
But...

02:20.720 --> 02:22.080
Bring the heat of the fire down! Down!

02:22.080 --> 02:22.870
R-Right...

02:24.650 --> 02:27.120
...there isn't a single woman here.

02:27.120 --> 02:30.290
Women are transgressors 
who turned their backs on the will of God.

02:30.290 --> 02:35.050
Which is why they are not allowed to make 
the sacred food, sugar confections.

02:35.050 --> 02:36.150
Transgressors?

02:36.610 --> 02:42.430
When God created a woman and a man, 
the wish was for them to rule over the earth.

02:42.720 --> 02:45.800
However, the human woman 
fell in love with the king of the fairies,

02:45.800 --> 02:47.700
and ended up vowing to serve him.

02:48.170 --> 02:50.140
The one who cleansed us 
of that woman's crime...

02:50.140 --> 02:52.040
and freed humanity from the fairies...

02:52.040 --> 02:54.970
creating a world in alignment 
with God's wishes...

02:54.970 --> 02:56.900
was Ancestor King Cedric.

02:58.420 --> 03:02.520
Sounds like you skipped out 
on the church's rest-day school.

03:03.120 --> 03:04.770
I'm sorry.

03:04.770 --> 03:07.360
Well, it's only a story.

03:07.360 --> 03:12.080
Among artisans, it's remained the reason 
that women shouldn't meddle in this work,

03:13.000 --> 03:17.250
but I think it's just that this work is 
physically more difficult for women.

03:22.840 --> 03:25.220
So, you've finally come, Hingley.

03:31.270 --> 03:32.310
<i>Jonas.</i>

03:33.830 --> 03:36.820
Well, your lot just doesn't seem 
to pass information along, you see...

03:36.820 --> 03:38.310
Mister Radcliffe.

03:39.300 --> 03:42.400
I see you still don't mind 
your words as you should.

03:42.400 --> 03:43.630
<i>Radcliffe?</i>

03:43.630 --> 03:47.120
<i>Then, this man is the master here... 
Marcus Radcliffe?</i>

03:47.120 --> 03:49.920
It's your own fault for not informing 
the Silver Sugar Viscount

03:49.920 --> 03:51.580
when you change residences.

03:51.580 --> 03:53.960
Not my problem. Give me some work.

03:53.960 --> 03:56.000
I need silver sugar.

03:56.920 --> 04:00.940
We'll have you oversee the refinement 
of the silver sugar in its entirety,

04:00.940 --> 04:02.970
together with Elliott Collins.

04:02.970 --> 04:04.510
Elliott?

04:04.510 --> 04:08.320
Isn't he acting as the head of 
the Paige workshop right now?

04:08.320 --> 04:10.240
He's late after going out without leave.

04:10.240 --> 04:11.710
That louse...

04:11.710 --> 04:13.440
I'll go get started first!

04:14.340 --> 04:16.780
So, you're Anne Halford?

04:16.780 --> 04:17.650
Yes, sir.

04:17.650 --> 04:21.400
I am the head of the Radcliffe 
Workshop, Marcus Radcliffe.

04:21.400 --> 04:24.530
It seems you've taken quite good 
care of my nephew, Jonas.

04:27.880 --> 04:30.920
I hear that you wish 
to participate in the Exhibition,

04:30.920 --> 04:33.680
but if your work isn't equivalent 
to that of the other artisans,

04:33.680 --> 04:35.600
you will not receive any sugar apples.

04:35.600 --> 04:38.780
I will do the work properly. 
That is why I have come here.

04:38.780 --> 04:41.660
The quantity of silver sugar 
we are processing is different here.

04:42.260 --> 04:45.070
The heavy stone mortars, 
the ladles and paddles...

04:45.070 --> 04:47.390
Can you move them as a man can?

04:47.390 --> 04:48.850
Yes, I can.

04:49.800 --> 04:52.310
Pluck alone won't get the work done.

04:52.310 --> 04:55.850
Do not be a hindrance. 
Be useful. That is all.

04:56.280 --> 04:57.340
Understood.

04:58.220 --> 05:00.650
Jonas, make sure to keep your wits about you.

05:00.650 --> 05:03.190
Just like Kieth, she is a powerful opponent.

05:03.650 --> 05:05.470
I understand, Uncle.

05:05.470 --> 05:09.120
If at this year's Exhibition, 
you fall behind this girl again,

05:09.120 --> 05:12.560
know that the only candidate for 
the next head of the workshop will be Kieth.

05:12.560 --> 05:13.540
Yes, sir.

05:13.950 --> 05:15.240
Do well.

05:17.440 --> 05:19.530
You seem to have quite 
a few difficulties of your own.

05:19.530 --> 05:21.260
I didn't ask for your opinion.

05:21.260 --> 05:23.740
Well then, I will go and work now.

05:23.740 --> 05:27.240
Do as you like. 
My uncle said it was all right.

05:27.240 --> 05:28.100
Then I will.

05:28.100 --> 05:29.430
Huh? Anne!

05:30.980 --> 05:32.060
Kat!

05:32.060 --> 05:34.920
I'm joining the workers. 
Please direct me as to what to do.

05:34.920 --> 05:35.830
Huh?

05:35.830 --> 05:36.770
Oh!

05:37.120 --> 05:38.780
Looking good there.

05:38.780 --> 05:40.750
It's easier to move around like this!

05:41.580 --> 05:43.760
We're shorthanded on the big cauldron.

05:43.760 --> 05:44.350
Go.

05:44.350 --> 05:45.140
Yes, sir!

05:46.400 --> 05:48.020
Right, here we go!

05:48.740 --> 05:50.540
You work in the background.

05:49.080 --> 05:50.540
What're you doing?!

05:50.540 --> 05:52.330
Let me go...

05:50.540 --> 05:52.330
The wagons will be leaving soon.

05:52.700 --> 05:55.930
Get on one of them 
and help harvest the sugar apples.

05:57.040 --> 05:58.800
What? With this guy?

05:58.800 --> 06:00.080
Huh? What is it?

06:00.080 --> 06:02.480
We've got work to do! Let's go!

06:02.480 --> 06:04.780
Those who do not work should not eat!

06:04.780 --> 06:07.420
Sithril, you sure are a hard worker.

06:07.420 --> 06:09.050
The name's <i>Mithril</i>!

06:09.050 --> 06:10.920
Don't fall asleep!

06:10.920 --> 06:12.010
Change out!

06:12.480 --> 06:13.760
Coming in!

06:20.450 --> 06:21.990
It's really hot!

06:22.520 --> 06:23.440
Hey!

06:23.790 --> 06:25.610
A woman's not gonna be able to move that!

06:26.090 --> 06:27.210
I will be fine!

06:32.840 --> 06:33.530
Hey!

06:33.530 --> 06:35.990
Women shouldn't interfere! You're in the way!

06:37.750 --> 06:41.910
Hey now, girls shouldn't be up here.

06:42.630 --> 06:46.200
If you fell and scarred your face, 
that would be terrible.

06:46.200 --> 06:47.130
Who are you?

06:47.130 --> 06:50.580
If I had to say, then I suppose 
I'm the ally of all women.

06:53.920 --> 06:56.100
Will you come have tea with me sometime?

06:56.590 --> 06:57.610
Yes?

06:57.610 --> 07:00.010
So, you're finally here, huh? Elliott?

07:01.360 --> 07:03.770
Your eye is just as good as ever, huh?

07:03.770 --> 07:06.020
<i>This is Elliott Collins?</i>

07:06.520 --> 07:09.720
<i>He's the silver sugar master who's standing 
in for the master of the Paige Workshop?</i>

07:10.160 --> 07:12.570
You there. You aren't 
a sugar artisan, are you?

07:12.570 --> 07:14.030
What? Yes, I am.

07:15.970 --> 07:17.490
Hey! Elliott!

07:17.880 --> 07:21.680
Why'd you bring a woman who 
isn't an artisan here? Get to work!

07:21.680 --> 07:23.960
No, before that, apologize for being late!

07:23.960 --> 07:28.250
You're being rude. This is the young lady 
of the Paige Workshop, you know?

07:28.250 --> 07:29.970
What? The Paige Workshop's...

07:31.620 --> 07:35.080
I am Glen Paige's daughter, Bridget.

07:35.080 --> 07:37.100
And why are you here?

07:37.100 --> 07:40.930
She's my fiancée. And she's come to visit me.

07:40.930 --> 07:44.680
No, I haven't. I'm here 
to help around the kitchen.

07:44.680 --> 07:47.720
There are other ladies here 
other than me, aren't there?

07:47.720 --> 07:49.440
But that's all just for show.

07:49.440 --> 07:53.370
She's actually here to cheer me on 
as I work my hardest!

07:53.370 --> 07:55.420
You haven't worked at all yet.

07:55.420 --> 07:57.200
And why are you just standing around?

07:57.200 --> 07:59.100
Oh. Right, sir!

08:10.660 --> 08:12.120
Guys...

08:14.390 --> 08:16.120
What's the meaning of those faces?

08:17.880 --> 08:19.770
Let anyone work who's
 willing to do the work!

08:42.740 --> 08:46.780
You could let her do some work 
that's a little more ladylike.

08:47.880 --> 08:49.520
Work that's ladylike?

08:49.520 --> 08:53.320
You know, cleaning or 
serving tea... or chatting with me.

08:53.320 --> 08:55.870
Chatting with you is not a job.

08:55.870 --> 08:58.780
Besides, she's a genuine artisan.

08:58.780 --> 09:00.810
She's been acknowledged as an artisan?

09:01.600 --> 09:02.840
Even though she's a woman?

09:06.040 --> 09:08.520
Something that dumb 
is irrelevant in this day and age.

09:08.520 --> 09:10.300
It's obvious that it's impossible,

09:11.210 --> 09:13.770
but she's still working 
so feverishly. It's laughable.

09:13.770 --> 09:16.990
Elliott, I'm going into town for a bit.

09:16.990 --> 09:18.880
Oh! Then, I'll go too!

09:18.880 --> 09:21.290
You and I are having a meeting, starting now.

09:21.290 --> 09:22.450
What?!

09:23.360 --> 09:25.660
<i>Kat has given me this chance.</i>

09:26.170 --> 09:27.620
<i>If I can't do this,</i>

09:27.930 --> 09:30.090
<i>then I won't get any sugar apples!</i>

09:31.380 --> 09:33.290
<i>I will make silver sugar...</i>

09:33.680 --> 09:35.180
<i>so that I can create my piece!</i>

09:41.450 --> 09:42.220
Here.

09:42.220 --> 09:43.470
Thank you.

09:43.900 --> 09:44.990
Here you are.

09:44.990 --> 09:46.680
Got it. Thanks.

09:51.080 --> 09:51.880
Here.

09:52.640 --> 09:54.030
Can I get an extra-large serving?

09:54.030 --> 09:56.400
No. The portions are predetermined.

09:56.960 --> 09:58.410
Here. This is all you get.

09:59.270 --> 10:00.520
Next, please.

10:03.110 --> 10:04.360
May I have some, please?

10:14.710 --> 10:16.340
You're a girl.

10:16.720 --> 10:18.580
How can you dress yourself like that?

10:19.230 --> 10:20.600
Please, may I have some food?

10:20.600 --> 10:22.540
The rule is one plate per person.

10:23.100 --> 10:24.350
I have companions.

10:24.920 --> 10:26.890
I'd like enough for them, too, please.

10:28.180 --> 10:29.730
It's all right.

10:30.190 --> 10:31.520
Please give her what she asked for.

10:31.520 --> 10:32.550
Kieth.

10:41.120 --> 10:42.520
I will have some food.

10:43.450 --> 10:45.790
Oh. O-Of course.

10:47.880 --> 10:49.020
What's wrong?

10:49.020 --> 10:49.820
Nothing.

10:52.940 --> 10:54.110
Here you are.

10:54.110 --> 10:55.420
Thank you.

10:55.790 --> 10:57.050
We're going back to our room.

10:57.050 --> 10:59.480
All right. Thank you, Kieth.

10:59.480 --> 11:00.810
You're very welcome.

11:01.900 --> 11:02.700
Challe.

11:36.750 --> 11:38.000
Yes?

11:38.300 --> 11:39.370
Jonas?

11:39.370 --> 11:42.220
I only came because my uncle told me to.

11:42.630 --> 11:46.590
He said that the sugar apples from 
today's harvest are in the storehouse.

11:46.590 --> 11:48.600
If you're planning 
to enter the Exhibition, then...

11:48.600 --> 11:50.060
He's letting me have some?

11:50.870 --> 11:52.980
So now I've told you, all right?

11:54.320 --> 11:56.480
Challe, I'll be right back!

12:01.270 --> 12:02.260
That's right.

12:03.300 --> 12:06.300
If she doesn't become 
a silver sugar master this year...

12:07.280 --> 12:09.480
<i>then she may not ever be able to.</i>

12:14.130 --> 12:16.360
Now I'll be able to make silver sugar.

12:17.310 --> 12:18.540
I'm so glad.

12:51.680 --> 12:54.940
Challe, aren't I heavy?

12:54.940 --> 12:58.280
It's fine. You are a scarecrow, after all.

12:58.280 --> 13:01.350
What are you saying? That's so mean...

13:33.450 --> 13:34.860
Do you want to be away from me?

13:37.320 --> 13:40.940
I suppose the one who didn't want us 
to be separated was me.

13:57.730 --> 13:59.050
How awful.

14:01.620 --> 14:04.780
To think she makes you 
work this late at night.

14:07.700 --> 14:08.530
Wait!

14:08.940 --> 14:12.460
If, by chance, you don't like 
being made to serve that girl,

14:12.460 --> 14:14.490
I could buy you from her.

14:15.590 --> 14:19.210
I wouldn't make you work late 
at night like this.

14:19.210 --> 14:22.460
No, I wouldn't ever order you to do anything.

14:22.460 --> 14:26.010
I'll let you live in a nice room 
and give you lots of sugar confections.

14:27.160 --> 14:29.180
So, I will buy you and...

14:32.010 --> 14:33.970
You plan to keep me as a pet?

14:33.970 --> 14:34.950
What?

14:37.800 --> 14:40.540
Your assistance is unwanted, human.

14:42.230 --> 14:46.720
6 Days Later

14:44.640 --> 14:47.230
How long is it gonna take you 
to skim that scum off?

14:47.230 --> 14:49.450
But if we don't skim it all off, 
it will make the sugar bitter.

14:49.720 --> 14:53.450
That's enough already! 
Hurry up and boil the next batch!

14:54.410 --> 14:57.630
It's gonna get mixed in with stuff 
from another cauldron later anyway,

14:57.630 --> 14:59.460
so there's no point!

14:59.460 --> 15:04.100
But... if the quality 
lowers little by little like this...

15:05.030 --> 15:07.450
then when it's all combined 
together, it will be truly awful.

15:07.450 --> 15:08.760
Oh, just pipe down.

15:08.760 --> 15:12.540
In any case, this year's silver sugar 
is all gonna be mass produced anyway.

15:12.540 --> 15:15.180
No one cares about the quality!

15:15.890 --> 15:18.740
In any case? No one cares?

15:19.650 --> 15:24.440
Then, will next year's sugar confections 
be made from this "no one cares" silver sugar?

15:25.510 --> 15:27.690
Will all the people who buy 
sugar confections next year...

15:28.300 --> 15:30.240
be buying confections of inferior quality?

15:31.220 --> 15:33.930
Even though it may be something 
they only buy once in their lifetimes,

15:33.930 --> 15:36.140
something incredibly precious?

15:37.200 --> 15:39.770
There's no need to say all that.

15:39.770 --> 15:42.790
If keeping quiet meant that I could make 
good silver sugar, then that's what I'd do!

15:43.880 --> 15:45.590
I do not approve of this.

15:45.930 --> 15:48.360
Making sugar confections with that mindset...

15:48.360 --> 15:49.390
it's just wrong!

15:49.390 --> 15:50.950
What did you say?

15:51.580 --> 15:52.130
Anne.

15:53.000 --> 15:54.460
It's time for your break, isn't it?

15:54.460 --> 15:55.180
What?!

16:02.660 --> 16:04.150
Calm down.

16:04.650 --> 16:07.770
The ones overseeing everything 
are Mister Hingley and Mister Collins.

16:07.770 --> 16:10.730
They know that doing things 
that way isn't good.

16:10.730 --> 16:12.620
Orders will come through soon.

16:12.620 --> 16:13.270
Oh.

16:14.360 --> 16:16.030
I see.

16:16.030 --> 16:18.470
Of course. We are talking 
about Kat after all.

16:19.210 --> 16:22.410
I feel like such an idiot.

16:22.410 --> 16:24.350
You’ve just used up all
 your patience, that’s all.

16:24.350 --> 16:25.470
But...

16:25.470 --> 16:28.510
Don't worry. You're doing a good job.

16:28.510 --> 16:31.800
And that's why Mister Radcliffe 
gave you sugar apples.

16:31.800 --> 16:35.530
How is that going? Have you 
finished processing your allotment?

16:36.040 --> 16:40.250
Yes. Last night. 
I managed to process four barrels' worth.

16:40.720 --> 16:43.690
Then it's finally time to 
start crafting your piece, isn't it?

16:44.060 --> 16:47.400
Between you and I, who will
 make the better piece?

16:48.260 --> 16:50.180
You're really amazing, Kieth.

16:50.850 --> 16:54.570
I haven't been able to think 
about my piece at all yet.

16:54.570 --> 16:56.610
But there's something 
you want to make, isn't there?

16:57.040 --> 16:59.780
Yes, there is, but...

17:02.200 --> 17:06.120
May I ask? Why did you want 
to have Challe as your model?

17:06.640 --> 17:07.830
Well...

17:08.350 --> 17:14.150
because the royal family tends to 
favor sugar confections with a fairy motif.

17:15.640 --> 17:19.320
If you visit the head temple of the kingdom's 
religion, the Church of Saint Lewiston Bell,

17:19.320 --> 17:22.070
there's a book about the royal 
family and sugar confections.

17:22.810 --> 17:23.770
What do you think?

17:24.200 --> 17:25.260
It's beautiful.

17:26.400 --> 17:30.940
Yes. It's amazing. Challe's 
essence really comes through.

17:31.910 --> 17:37.940
Challe's hair, his eyelashes, his eyes... 
You're going to craft them so delicately here.

17:38.810 --> 17:41.480
I just know it's going to be 
a truly wonderful sugar confection.

17:41.910 --> 17:45.870
Really? Hearing you say that 
makes me very happy.

17:49.440 --> 17:53.780
<i>If I had made it, would the results 
have been this good?</i>

17:54.880 --> 17:56.780
<i>Now that I've seen something like this...</i>

17:58.070 --> 18:00.330
<i>What could I make that would...</i>

18:02.450 --> 18:03.310
What?

18:03.310 --> 18:05.320
Is that... Challe?

18:06.770 --> 18:07.770
What?

18:08.170 --> 18:09.370
Miss Bridget?

18:10.090 --> 18:12.690
I'm sorry to call you out here like this.

18:12.690 --> 18:16.780
You aren't serving that girl, Anne, are you?

18:16.780 --> 18:18.660
And in spite of that, I...

18:18.660 --> 18:20.530
That's enough. Forget it happened.

18:20.530 --> 18:21.960
Wait! Please, listen!

18:26.210 --> 18:27.420
I...

18:34.260 --> 18:37.510
I have a fiancé that my family 
decided upon for me.

18:38.210 --> 18:40.270
I wasn't in love with anyone.

18:40.270 --> 18:43.990
I didn't even understand 
what love was, really, so it didn't bother me.

18:44.510 --> 18:46.470
But the other day, when I saw you...

18:47.070 --> 18:50.190
my heart raced so fast 
I didn't know what to do.

18:50.850 --> 18:54.650
I love you. I truly love you!

18:57.160 --> 18:58.920
Anne? Is something wrong?

18:59.560 --> 19:01.320
No, it's nothing!

19:01.320 --> 19:04.620
We should go. If we stay away from 
our work for too long, Kat will yell at us.

19:04.620 --> 19:05.780
Stop that.

19:06.490 --> 19:09.560
If you really do have your freedom,

19:09.560 --> 19:12.070
then you can do whatever you like 
of your own will, right?

19:12.840 --> 19:15.860
What of it? Are you saying 
we should just kiss, then?

19:16.400 --> 19:20.270
If I were human, would you have 
used this method?

19:20.270 --> 19:21.010
What?

19:22.290 --> 19:25.930
<i>Why were Challe and Miss Bridget...</i>

19:26.360 --> 19:30.890
If you had been talking to Kieth Powell 
or Alph Hingley, would you have done this?

19:30.890 --> 19:33.900
No, I wouldn't. I would be too embarrassed.

19:35.400 --> 19:39.150
Which means that you're not 
embarrassed now because I am a fairy.

19:39.150 --> 19:39.920
What?

19:39.920 --> 19:42.910
It's no different from buying 
a companion fairy for you.

19:42.910 --> 19:44.030
You have it all wrong.

19:44.030 --> 19:47.720
If you want me, then steal 
my wing and give me an order.

19:47.720 --> 19:49.250
Command me to love you.

19:53.420 --> 19:55.160
Anne, what's wrong?

19:55.160 --> 19:57.000
It's nothing.

19:59.840 --> 20:00.800
What?

20:01.160 --> 20:03.430
Let's go. We're running!

20:03.430 --> 20:04.700
Wait!

20:28.520 --> 20:31.050
Honestly! What was that all of a sudden?

20:31.050 --> 20:32.510
We're about to start work.

20:32.510 --> 20:35.110
You have to run so you can leave 
all your worries behind first.

20:36.660 --> 20:39.250
If you need someone to listen, 
I can do that much for you.

20:40.460 --> 20:43.580
Focus on your work. Make something good.

20:43.580 --> 20:45.340
And then compete with me.

20:45.340 --> 20:46.320
All right?

20:46.320 --> 20:46.970
Yes.

20:47.720 --> 20:48.440
Good.

20:59.400 --> 21:05.030
The Young Lady of the Paige Workshop

21:16.290 --> 21:20.620
<i>Is it just like the dreams we dream at night?</i>

21:21.490 --> 21:26.760
<i>Do we give names to our other dreams because,</i>

21:26.760 --> 21:30.300
<i>Just as our night dreams 
are forgotten upon waking,</i>

21:30.300 --> 21:37.370
<i>If they aren't held dear, 
they will disappear?</i>

21:37.370 --> 21:48.510
<i>No, it's because they aren't things 
that only special people can see</i>

21:48.510 --> 21:49.240
<i>That day</i>

21:49.240 --> 21:53.690
<i>I reached out again and again</i>

21:53.690 --> 21:59.250
<i>I failed to catch that shining fruit, and yet</i>

21:59.250 --> 22:04.750
<i>I'll reach out once more</i>

22:04.750 --> 22:09.050
<i>If I make my wishes come true myself</i>

22:09.050 --> 22:14.880
<i>I just know it will make you smile</i>

22:14.880 --> 22:26.360
<i>That's why I'm able to say I'm not giving up</i>

22:36.160 --> 22:40.080
<b>That Which Should Be Made</b>
